IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`

-- Section 202(a)(1), (2), (4), (5), (6), (7): who extended compensation is for, and the
-- conditions beside the work test. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- The Act speaks to the State law: "a State law shall provide the payment of extended
-- compensation shall be made ... to individuals who ...". The relation is between the individual
-- (who holds a claim under the State law that meets these terms) and the State (which bears the
-- duty to pay); paragraphs (3) to (5) take that claim away in the cases they list, and (6) denies
-- the State the federal share of a payment made in those cases.
-- out of text: the State law's definitions of benefit year, base period, week, weekly benefit
-- amount and insured wages (s 205(5), (6), (11)); the State law's choice of method under (a)(5);
-- the State law's disqualifications and when it ends them (a)(4); the unemployment compensation
-- law of another State or of Canada, and other Federal law (a)(1). All are plain inputs.

§ `Section 202(a): the State law requirements`

§§ `202(a)(1): who extended compensation is payable to`

-- src:26 | For purposes of the preceding sentence, an individual shall have exhausted his rights to regular compensation under a State law (A) when no payments of regular compensation can be made under such law because such individual has received all regular compensation available to him based on employment or wages during his base period
-- src:26 | or (B) when his rights to such compensation have terminated by reason of the expiration of the benefit year with respect to which such rights existed.
@ref s 202(a)(1), second sentence (src:26)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      benefitYear IS A `Benefit year`
      position IS A `Regular compensation position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual has exhausted all rights to regular compensation` week benefitYear position MEANS
        position's `received all the regular compensation available on the base period employment or wages`
    OR  benefitYear's `last day of the benefit year` LESS THAN week

-- src:26 | who have no rights to regular compensation with respect to such week under such law or any other State unemployment compensation law or to compensation under any other Federal law and are not receiving compensation with respect to such week under the unemployment compensation law of Canada.
@ref s 202(a)(1), first sentence (src:26)
GIVEN position IS A `Regular compensation position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` position MEANS
        (NOT position's `rights to regular compensation for the week under the State law`)
    AND (NOT position's `rights to regular compensation for the week under another State's unemployment compensation law`)
    AND (NOT position's `compensation for the week under another Federal law`)
    AND (NOT position's `receiving compensation for the week under the unemployment compensation law of Canada`)

-- src:26 | a State law shall provide the payment of extended compensation shall be made, for any week of unemployment which begins in the individual’s eligibility period, to individuals who have exhausted all rights to regular compensation under the State law
@ref s 202(a)(1), first sentence (src:26)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      benefitYear IS A `Benefit year`
      position IS A `Regular compensation position`
      inEligibilityPeriod IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the State law must provide payment of extended compensation for the week` week benefitYear position inEligibilityPeriod MEANS
        inEligibilityPeriod
    AND `the individual has exhausted all rights to regular compensation` week benefitYear position
    AND `the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` position

§§ `202(a)(2): the State law's terms for regular claims`

-- src:27 | “(2) Except where inconsistent with the provisions of this title, the terms and conditions of the State law which apply to claims for regular compensation and to the payment thereof shall apply to claims for extended compensation and to the payment thereof.
@ref s 202(a)(2) (src:27)
GIVEN `the State rule is inconsistent with the provisions of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a State rule for regular compensation claims applies to extended compensation claims` `the State rule is inconsistent with the provisions of this title` MEANS
    NOT `the State rule is inconsistent with the provisions of this title`

§§ `202(a)(4): disqualifications that the State law would end`

-- src:52 | “(4) No provision of State law which terminates a disqualification for voluntarily leaving employment, being discharged for misconduct, or refusing suitable employment shall apply for purposes of determining eligibility for extended compensation unless such termination is based upon employment subsequent to the date of such disqualification.
@ref s 202(a)(4) (src:52)
GIVEN disqualification IS A Disqualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the termination of the disqualification applies to eligibility for extended compensation` disqualification MEANS
        disqualification's `the State law has terminated the disqualification`
    AND disqualification's `the termination is based upon employment subsequent to the date of the disqualification`

-- src:52 | “(4) No provision of State law which terminates a disqualification for voluntarily leaving employment, being discharged for misconduct, or refusing suitable employment shall apply for purposes of determining eligibility for extended compensation unless such termination is based upon employment subsequent to the date of such disqualification.
@ref s 202(a)(4) (src:52)
GIVEN disqualification IS A Disqualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the disqualification still bars extended compensation` disqualification MEANS
    NOT (`the termination of the disqualification applies to eligibility for extended compensation` disqualification)

-- src:52 | “(4) No provision of State law which terminates a disqualification for voluntarily leaving employment, being discharged for misconduct, or refusing suitable employment shall apply for purposes of determining eligibility for extended compensation unless such termination is based upon employment subsequent to the date of such disqualification.
@ref s 202(a)(4) (src:52)
GIVEN disqualifications IS A LIST OF Disqualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a disqualification still bars extended compensation` disqualifications MEANS
    any (GIVEN disqualification YIELD `the disqualification still bars extended compensation` disqualification) disqualifications

§§ `202(a)(5): the employment the individual must have had`

-- src:53 | the individual had 20 weeks of full-time insured employment, or the equivalent in insured wages.
@ref s 202(a)(5), first sentence (src:53)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual had 20 weeks of full-time insured employment` employment MEANS
    employment's `weeks of full-time insured employment in the base period` AT LEAST 20

-- src:53 | earnings covered by the State law for compensation purposes which exceed 40 times the individual’s most recent weekly benefit amount
@ref s 202(a)(5), second sentence (src:53)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the earnings exceed 40 times the most recent weekly benefit amount` employment MEANS
    employment's `earnings covered by the State law in the base period` GREATER THAN
        (40 TIMES employment's `most recent weekly benefit amount`)

-- src:53 | or 1½ times the individual’s insured wages in that calendar quarter of the base period in which the individual’s insured wages were the highest
@ref s 202(a)(5), second sentence (src:53)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the earnings exceed one and a half times the highest quarter` employment MEANS
    employment's `earnings covered by the State law in the base period` GREATER THAN
        (1.5 TIMES employment's `insured wages in the calendar quarter of the base period in which they were highest`)

-- src:53 | The State shall by law provide which one or more of the foregoing methods of measuring employment and earnings shall be used in that State.
@ref s 202(a)(5), third sentence (src:53)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the State law has chosen at least one method` employment MEANS
        employment's `the State law uses the 20 weeks of full-time insured employment method`
    OR  employment's `the State law uses the earnings above 40 times the weekly benefit amount method`
    OR  employment's `the State law uses the earnings above one and a half times the highest quarter method`

-- The individual meets the requirement if a method the State law uses is met. See the fork register
-- on "one or more" and on whether "exceed" governs both wage methods.
-- src:53 | an individual shall not be eligible for extended compensation unless, in the base period with respect to which the individual exhausted all rights to regular compensation under the State law
@ref s 202(a)(5) (src:53)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
GIVETH A `Result of the employment requirement`
`the result of the employment requirement` employment MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the State law has chosen at least one method` employment)
             THEN `the State law has chosen no method, which section 202(a)(5) requires it to do`
           IF (  (   employment's `the State law uses the 20 weeks of full-time insured employment method`
                 AND `the individual had 20 weeks of full-time insured employment` employment)
               OR (   employment's `the State law uses the earnings above 40 times the weekly benefit amount method`
                  AND `the earnings exceed 40 times the most recent weekly benefit amount` employment)
               OR (   employment's `the State law uses the earnings above one and a half times the highest quarter method`
                  AND `the earnings exceed one and a half times the highest quarter` employment))
             THEN `the individual has the required employment`
           OTHERWISE `the individual lacks the required employment`

§§ `202(a)(7): when paragraphs (3) and (4) do not apply`

-- src:55 | “(7) Paragraphs (3) and (4) shall not apply to weeks of unemployment beginning after March 6, 1993, and before January 1, 1995, and no provision of State law in conformity with such paragraphs shall apply during such period.
@ref s 202(a)(7) (src:55)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` week MEANS
        week AT MOST `6 March 1993`
    OR  week AT LEAST `1 January 1995`

§§ `202(a)(6): the federal share of a payment the rules of (3), (4) and (5) would not allow`

-- src:54 | “(6) No payment shall be made under this Act [see Short Title of 1970 Amendment note set out under section 3311 of this title] to any State in respect of any extended compensation or sharable regular compensation paid to any individual for any week if, under the rules of paragraphs (3), (4), and (5), extended compensation would not have been payable to such individual for such week.
@ref s 202(a)(6) (src:54)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      workTestBars IS A BOOLEAN
      disqualificationBars IS A BOOLEAN
      employmentResult IS A `Result of the employment requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` week workTestBars disqualificationBars employmentResult MEANS
        (    `paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` week
         AND (workTestBars OR disqualificationBars))
    OR  (NOT (employmentResult EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`))
